WEBVTT

00:02:57.446 --> 00:03:00.613
She is treated with surgery,
chemotherapy and radiation.

00:03:00.637 --> 00:03:01.821
She goes home.

00:03:01.845 --> 00:03:02.996
Two years later,

00:03:03.020 --> 00:03:06.194
she comes back with stage 3C
ovarian cancer, unfortunately;

00:03:06.218 --> 00:03:08.655
treated again with surgery
and chemotherapy.

00:03:08.679 --> 00:03:10.933
She comes back three years later at age 42

00:03:10.957 --> 00:03:13.314
with more ovarian cancer,
more chemotherapy.

00:03:13.338 --> 00:03:14.807
Six months later,

00:03:14.831 --> 00:03:18.655
she comes back
with acute myeloid leukemia.

00:03:19.559 --> 00:03:22.565
She goes into respiratory failure
and dies eight days later.

00:03:22.589 --> 00:03:24.947
So first: the way in which
this woman was treated,

00:03:24.971 --> 00:03:28.414
in as little as 10 years,
will look like bloodletting.

00:03:28.438 --> 00:03:31.263
And it's because of people
like my colleague, Rick Wilson,